      "pins": ["U1.VO", "M2B.3V3", "M2B.5V0"],
      "nets": ["+3V3", "+5V"],
      "observed": "U1, an AZ1117-3.3 LDO, has its VO pin connected to +3V3, and M2B's 3V3 pin is also connected to +3V3. M2B's 5V0 pin is powered from +5V, so the DevKit's onboard 3.3 V regulator is powered while its 3V3 output is tied to the separate U1 output.",
      "expected": "Use one 3.3 V source for the shared rail, or keep the external LDO output separate from the DevKit's onboard-regulator output. Do not parallel the two regulator outputs without an arrangement specifically designed for it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "U1 AZ1117-3.3; VI; VO; +3V3",
          "sheet and page": "Sheet 1/1, POWER TRAIN, page 1"
        },
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "M2B ESP32-C6-DEVKIT; 5V0; 3V3; +5V; +3V3",
          "sheet and page": "Sheet 1/1, POWER TRAIN, page 1"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "U2 — AZ1117-3.3 (Diodes Inc.) | 5 V → 3.3 V LDO, 1 A"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The external LDO and the DevKit's onboard 3.3 V regulator may drive against each other, causing excess current, unstable 3.3 V operation, or damage to a regulator.",
      "confidence": 0.93
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic connects the external AZ1117 output and the ESP32 DevKit's 3V3 pin to the same rail while also powering the DevKit from 5 V. This risks paralleling two regulator outputs."
}

